it depends on how critical this machine will be once it is in
production.

there are several things I consider when deciding weather to run linux
or osf on my boxes.

1. how critical the system is for being up ..  how much downtime
is       
   acceptable.

2. what features of the operating system are required. ie I use the
advfs on my osf boxes to allow me to add more drive space for the mail
spool without having to make a newfs and then copy mailboxes etc..
(linux cant do this)

3. what dec box you get, if it doesnt have the SRM console then you wont
be able to boot OSF.

Kelly



