Last summber I needed a loopback on the serial cables. I went to a local
electronics shop and paid $2.00. A solution is to take 2 standard modem
cables, (the ones without moulded connectors). Remove the casing on
both. On one of the cable connectors, remove the wires going to the
comm2 pins. Cut off the other connector (make sure you know which wires
are which. Take the appropriate wires and connect them to the comm2
pins. You now have a Y cable. Basically, you only have 6 or 7 wires to
connect. You might also check with some of the 3rd party vendors, such
as Steve Gaudet at DCG computers (http://www.dcginc.com/). You can get
the parts at just about any computer store. 
