Hello,

I'm trying to install Red Hat 5.0-Alpha on an XL-266 Alpha system, using
Milo, boot, and ramdisk diskettes generated from the appropriate images
on the distribution CD, but the kernel hangs upon bootup, just after the
message '"turning on virtual addressing and jumping to the Linux
kernel". This error is also mentioned in the manual, p. 246. I've used
the XLT images for the Milo and the kernel disks, and rebuilt them
repeatedly, to no avail. The system has a Toshiba SCSI 2 CDROM and a
Quantum Fireball SCSI harddisk. I'm using a generic IBM SVGA monitor,
without any 'smart' frills. There are no further external peripherals
attached. The processor is an AXP21064, with 32 MB RAM, the video board
a Matrox Millennium (PCI, 2 MB, with VGA support enabled). 

Judging by the explanation in the manual, the latter could be the cause
of the problem, as Matrox isn't fully supported by RH 5.0 Alpha, but it
is recognised by Milo as a VGA device, and Milo itself boots up fine,
through the Windows NT ARC firmware interface. The crash doestn't occur
until the kernel itself is loaded. I know that the XLT kernel is
focussed on AlphaBIOS based systems (XL-300 and up), but it should
support the ARC based XL systems as well. I don't have a officially
supported VGA card to test whether the videoboard is responsible.

Any clues? 

Regards,
Marco



