>to install Redhat Linux 5.0.  Has anybody have any success installing
>Linux on an ALPHA XL300.  Any suggestions?
>I'll be trying to install Redhat Linux 4.2 to see if I have better luck.

Exactly how far are you getting? A couple of things to note: use the XLT
milo and kernel images (NOT XL), and see if that gets you further.
A problem I had on mine was that I couldn't boot using the CD-ROM as the
root filesystem. Got I/O errors reading the CD.

A workaround was to create a root floppy and install like that. CD-ROM has
been fine ever since. (Note that the same disk mounted as the root filesystem
perfectly in a friends (identical) XL-300. :-/)

>One other question for all you XL300 owners, do I have to use 70ns
>memory or can I use 60ns.  I tried 60ns simms but my computer didn't
>like it, don't know if I can use 60ns or if the memory's bad.

There's no problem with running 60ns memory, but it has to be FULL PARITY
memory. Ie, the cheaper memory that most PC vendors sell won't work.


