EmmanuelS (EmmanuelS@hol.fr) wrote:
: I ve put the patch in my directory /usr/src/linux and I do  
: gunzip < alpha.patch.gz | patch -p1.
: I have this question Reserved patch detected... Asume -R? [y]
: lot of times and  in the end I have file to patch:
: After I try to build my kernel but impossible why??

Because you're running what I'm running, which is RedHat 4.2.  The kernel
supplied in RH4.2 is apparently modified enough from the "stock" kernel
that the em86 patches won't apply.  This probably is true of *all* RH-
supplied kernels, but I cannot say this with authority; my experience is
with 4.2 only.
Last I asked about this, I was told it would be necessary to build from
*fresh* kernel source + Em86 patches.  I have not tried this, however.  I
don't have the time or the desire for pain right now... :)

good luck,
Jonathan



