called, surprisingly enough, "minlabel" plus some version markings
(1.2-2 is the current one).  Here is a relevant part of an output
from 'rmp -qiv minlabel':

Summary     : creates and edits Berkeley style disk labels
Description :
Hard drives on Alpha's are partitioned in one of two distinct ways, PC style
partitioning or BSD Unix style labeling. This program provides a way of
creating, viewing, and editing BSD labels on hard drives.

No idea where you were looking.

