mbkennel@yahoo.com (Matt Kennel) wrote:

> Does SPECfp test elementary functions at all?

Nope, and I told you why:  SPEC code (either int or fp) is not *allowed* to 
spend significant time in library routines, specifically because SPEC tries 
to measure reproducable performance.  If they would leave to much to (binary 
only) library routines, they would have a gaping hole in their procedures.

If you want to get a typical (that is: for the rest of us) speed up on Alpha 
vs Pentium, see: 
http://www.ec-nantes.fr/F_Serveur/Recherche/DMN/WWW/Hardware/Bench/res_65.htm
