>     - Things seem working fine on the c/c++ side,
>       but I am having big segmentation faults 
>       when running certains fortran subroutines
>       compiled with egcs g77 1.0.1

There are known bugs in egcs-1.0.1/g77 when using negative lower bounds in 
arrays.  This might be your problem.

On the Other Hand, segmentation faults can also be caused by using to much 
stack space.  Note that the default in g77 is to allocate arrays less than 
32K in size on the stack.  Read the documentation of your shell on how to 
enlarge that limit.

