Hi!!  (from Alessandro Mirone: alex@greco2.polytechnique.fr)

   I solved the problem:-)
 Answer: The generated shared library was too big!!!!!!!
I thought this problem had been solved in RH5.0,
 with RH4.2 the building of a too big library fails,
 but with 5.0 it is successful, unfortunately
 it explodes later at run-time.

 So I splitted (as I was used to do in RH4.2) the big
 lapack library in two smaller parts and the big segmentation 
faults
disappeared as soon.

Weird.. isn't?? But at least things are working now.
Might this problem be linked to the above stack space limitations?

Greetings

   almost got mad  
                    Alessandro




