: flags were -O3 -ffast-math and on x86 -malign-double,

As I mentioned before: on my limited testing of some "sin/cos rich"
Fortran code using -ffast-math actually noticeably harmed a performance.
On the other hand adding '-funroll-loops -fomit-frame-pointer'
had a substantial positive impact.

It is quite possible that running a few experiments one can arrive
with a set of "good" compilation flags for a given code.  They do not
have to be obvious.

  Michal




